        "summary": "A Claude Code skill. Type /graphify in Claude Code - it reads your files, builds a knowledge graph, and gives you back structure you didn't know was there. Fully multimodal. Drop in code, PDFs, markdown, screenshots, diagrams, whiteboard photos, even images in other languages - graphify uses Claude vision to extract concepts and relationships from all of it and connects them into one graph. Andrej Karpathy keeps a /raw folder where he drops papers, tweets, screenshots, and notes. graphify is the answer to that problem - 71.5x fewer tokens per query vs reading the raw files, persistent across sessions, honest about what it found vs guessed.",
